1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:11,010
We all know that having too much work and too much stress can lead to burnout, but did you know that the opposite can also be a problem?
我们都知道工作量过大、压力过大会导致精疲力竭，但你知道吗，相反的情况也可能是一个问题？

2
00:00:11,010 --> 00:00:17,110
Have you ever felt that your job was too easy and that everything was just a bit too boring?
你是否曾觉得自己的工作太轻松，一切都有些太无聊？

3
00:00:17,110 --> 00:00:21,390
If so, you might be suffering from rust out.
如果是这样，你可能正在遭受职业倦怠的困扰。

4
00:00:21,390 --> 00:00:28,090
Rust out happens when there isn't enough challenge to motivate you to keep going in your job.
职业倦怠发生在工作中缺乏足够的挑战来激励你持续前进的时候。

5
00:00:28,090 --> 00:00:33,070
Without some challenge, it can be hard to feel growth in your role.
没有一些挑战，就很难感受到自己在岗位上的成长。

6
00:00:33,070 --> 00:00:40,680
If a job has lots of repetitive and monotonous tasks, it can make it hard to see the purpose of a role.
如果一份工作有很多重复且单调的任务，就很难看清一个岗位的意义。

7
00:00:40,680 --> 00:00:47,700
Having a lower level of responsibility at work than before can also make it harder to feel fulfilled in a job.
工作中的责任水平比以前低，也会让人更难在工作中感到有成就感。

8
00:00:47,700 --> 00:00:53,050
This can affect people who have taken time out from their career for family or personal reasons.
这可能会影响到那些因家庭或个人原因而职业中断的人。

9
00:00:53,050 --> 00:00:59,260
If you think that you might be suffering from rust out, then there are a number of signs to watch out for.
如果你认为自己可能正遭受职业倦怠的困扰，那么有一些迹象需要注意。

10
00:00:59,260 --> 00:01:04,690
You might dread finding your schedule each week and not seeing anything stimulating on it.
你可能会害怕看到每周的日程安排，上面没有任何令人兴奋的内容。

11
00:01:04,690 --> 00:01:10,750
It might be that you often find yourself clock-watching at work, willing the time to pass.
你可能经常在工作中盯着时钟盼下班，希望时间快点过去。

12
00:01:10,750 --> 00:01:18,320
Focus and motivation can drop, leading you to get less done than you had before, or to make more mistakes.
注意力和积极性会下降，导致你比以前完成的工作更少，或者犯更多的错误。

13
00:01:18,320 --> 00:01:23,060
You may start to feel apathetic and disengaged towards your job.
你可能会开始对自己的工作感到冷漠和疏离。

14
00:01:23,060 --> 00:01:30,060
These feelings can lead to anxiety and depression which can then spread from work into people's personal lives.
这些感受可能导致焦虑和抑郁，然后从工作蔓延到人们的个人生活中。

15
00:01:30,060 --> 00:01:34,790
Finding yourself suffering from rust out can sometimes be an opportunity.
发现自己正遭受职业倦怠的困扰有时也可能是一个机会。

16
00:01:34,790 --> 00:01:38,090
Some experts suggest that self-awareness is key.
一些专家建议，自我意识是关键。

17
00:01:38,090 --> 00:01:46,670
By taking some time to realise what you are really looking for in work and life, you can take steps to re-discover your motivation.
花些时间意识到自己在工作和生活中真正想要的是什么，你就可以采取措施重新发现自己的动力。

18
00:01:46,670 --> 00:01:53,280
Setting yourself goals and allowing yourself to try new things can help you find a new purpose.
给自己设定目标，允许自己尝试新事物，可以帮助你找到新的意义。

19
00:01:53,280 --> 00:02:00,670
Considering what you really need for a job can also lead you to find a new one that's better suited to your goals in life.
考虑一份工作你真正需要什么，也可以引导你找到一份更适合你人生目标的新工作。
